<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saibai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1659</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Saibai Bhonsale, Saibai Nimbalkar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saibai was the first wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> state. A daughter of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nimbalkar">Nimbalkar</a> family of Phaltan, she married Shivaji as a child in 1640, linking his family to one of the oldest Maratha houses. She was the mother of Sambhaji, Shivaji's eldest son and successor, and died in 1659 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajgad">Rajgad</a>.</p></div>
